# Line endings. Every text file is LF in the repository AND in the working
# tree, on every platform. Without `eol=lf` a Windows checkout gets CRLF while
# tools that rewrite files (vitest snapshots, generated docs) write LF, so the
# file reads as modified the moment a test runs.
#
# There are no `.bat`/`.cmd`/`.ps1` scripts here. If any are added they must
# opt back in to CRLF, because the Windows shell needs it:
#     *.bat  text eol=crlf
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Wire-protocol frame fixtures: byte-exact, and a line-ending rewrite would
# silently corrupt them.
*.bin   binary
